---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title={`Your copy of the handbook — ${SITE.name}`}
  description="Download Building in British Columbia: What the Owner Is Responsible For."
  noindex={true}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-20 sm:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="annotation uppercase tracking-widest">Sent</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Here it is</h1>
      <p class="prose mt-5">
        A copy is on its way to your inbox. You can also take it straight from here.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-8">
        <a
          href="/downloads/bc-owners-handbook.pdf"
          class="inline-block border border-ink bg-ink px-6 py-3 text-base font-medium text-paper transition-colors hover:border-accent hover:bg-accent"
          download
        >
          Download the handbook (PDF)
        </a>
      </p>

      <p class="prose mt-10">
        Two chapters are worth reading first if you are short of time. <strong>Chapter 5</strong> covers the
        10% the Builders Lien Act requires you to withhold, and what happens to an owner who pays in full
        without retaining it. <strong>Appendix B</strong> is nine questions to ask before signing a
        construction contract — it takes four minutes and is the highest-return part of the guide.
      </p>

      <p class="prose mt-4">
        No newsletter follows this. If a question comes up while you are reading it, write to
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and a principal will answer — that is not a
        pipeline, it is two people and an inbox.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-10 max-w-prose text-sm leading-relaxed text-mid">
        This guide explains what the legislation requires. It is not legal advice. Consult a BC construction
        lawyer on your specific project.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
